  homeCapsEyebrow: 'CAPABILITIES',
  homeCapsTitle: 'Six facts you can check.',
  homeCapsLede: 'Every line maps to a specific behaviour in the file format, a public API or the user documentation. No adjectives stand in for evidence.',
  homeCap1Title: 'One file to hold',
  homeCap1Fact: 'The main file is a YDPG page file. Only WAL mode adds -wal and -shm companions, and after a checkpoint a backup is just the main file.',
  homeCap1Tag: 'YDPG · YYWL',
  homeCap2Title: 'In-process, no service',
  homeCap2Fact: 'Database.open("app.yydb") opens the file inside your application process. The library listens on no port and needs no resident process.',
  homeCap2Tag: 'IN-PROCESS',
  homeCap3Title: 'Schema travels with the file',
  homeCap3Fact: 'The VOS schema document is stored inside the .yydb file, so the CLI, clients and the engine read the same definition.',
  homeCap3Tag: 'VOS DOC',
  homeCap4Title: 'Folded after the WAL',
  homeCap4Fact: 'Commits are appended to YYWL first and folded on clean close or a threshold. checkpoint() writes the frames back to pages and clears companions.',
  homeCap4Tag: 'ATOMIC COMMIT',
  homeCap5Title: 'One language to read and write',
  homeCap5Fact: 'query takes a VOS read pipeline and returns plain objects. execute takes a VOS write program and has committed before it returns.',
  homeCap5Tag: 'QUERY · WRITE',
  homeCap6Title: 'Four hosts',
  homeCap6Fact: 'Four hosts share one VOS author surface: Node through the @yydb/yydb N-API, Rust through the yydb crate, the CLI calling the engine directly, and @yydb/light-db persisting the same WASM core in OPFS and addressing databases by name instead of file path.',
  homeCap6Tag: 'NODE · RUST · CLI · WASM',

  homeQuickEyebrow: 'REAL USAGE',
  homeQuickTitle: 'Once installed, this is all of it.',
  homeQuickLede: 'The snippet uses public API only and was run against this repo build on Node.js 24: publish a schema, write two records, read one, checkpoint, close. The terminal column is its verbatim output.',
  homeQuickInstall: 'INSTALL',
  homeQuickOutput: 'REAL OUTPUT',

  homeSpecEyebrow: 'DATA MODEL AND FORMAT',
  homeSpecTitle: 'One page file, two write paths.',
  homeSpecLede: 'Page and WAL numbers come from public yydb-formats constants. Checkpoint behaviour comes from the user documentation and the engine implementation.',
  homeSpec1Label: 'Page size',
  homeSpec1Value: '4096 B',
  homeSpec1Note: '16 B header · 4076 B payload · 4 B CRC32C trailer',
  homeSpec2Label: 'Page types',
  homeSpec2Value: '0x10 · 0x11',
  homeSpec2Note: '0x10 leaf, 0x11 internal. There is no third page type.',
  homeSpec3Label: 'File magics',
  homeSpec3Value: 'YDPG · YYWL · YYSH · YYBB',
  homeSpec3Note: 'Main file, WAL, SHM and CAS object segment magics',
  homeSpec4Label: 'Page check',
  homeSpec4Value: 'CRC32C',
  homeSpec4Note: 'A failed check means corruption. There is no skip-bad-page mode.',
  homeSpec5Label: 'WAL records',
  homeSpec5Value: '37 B · 13 B · 8 MiB',
  homeSpec5Note: '37 B WAL header, 13 B record header, 8 MiB per record',
  homeSpec6Label: 'Inline limit',
  homeSpec6Value: '1 KiB',
  homeSpec6Note: 'Above it the value becomes a CAS object reference. A single-file .yydb rejects overflow explicitly.',
  homeSpec7Label: 'Checkpoint',
  homeSpec7Value: 'Clean close or threshold',
  homeSpec7Note: 'checkpoint() folds the WAL and clears companions. Reopen replays complete transactions only.',

  homeBoundEyebrow: 'BOUNDARIES',
  homeBoundTitle: 'It also declines to do these things.',
  homeBoundLede: 'A boundary written as a contract is easier to check than a slogan. Each line describes current behaviour, not a future plan.',
  homeBound1Title: 'No network service',
  homeBound1Body: 'The library listens on no port. yydb serve is a separate command that binds 127.0.0.1:7700 by default and has no login layer.',
  homeBound2Title: 'No concurrent writers',
  homeBound2Body: 'The file database is protected by an OS exclusive lock. One writer at a time.',
  homeBound3Title: 'No clustering or auth',
  homeBound3Body: 'Clustering, tenancy, roles and audit belong to YYDS. YYDB is not its control plane or replica group.',
  homeBound4Title: 'No nested transactions',
  homeBound4Body: 'A transaction commits when the callback returns and rolls back when it throws. Merge nested logic at the outer level.',
  homeBound5Title: 'DDL stays outside transactions',
  homeBound5Body: 'Tables are published through the VOS schema document and do not commit with KV transactions.',
  homeBound6Title: 'SQLite files are read-only',
  homeBound6Body: '@yydb/sqlite reads format-3 snapshots only. It runs no SQL, recovers no WAL, and does not scan index B-trees, WITHOUT ROWID or virtual tables.',
  homeBound7Title: 'ANN is unreleased',
  homeBound7Body: 'Vector indexing remains on the roadmap and must not be relied on in production.',

  homeCmpEyebrow: 'COMPARISON',
  homeCmpTitle: 'Differences from SQLite, only what can be checked.',
  homeCmpLede: 'No like-for-like benchmark was run, so there is no performance claim here.',
